# 04 – Split-Tunnel Configuration

## 1. Overview

Split tunneling allows selected network traffic to travel through the WireGuard VPN while other internet traffic continues through the client's normal internet connection.

For this home lab, I configured split tunneling on my CachyOS Linux laptop to provide secure remote access to my home network through the OPNsense firewall.

The objective was to access internal devices and the OPNsense management interface remotely without sending all internet traffic through the VPN.

## 2. Network Configuration

| Component | IP Address / Network |
|---|---|
| OPNsense LAN | `192.168.1.1/24` |
| Home LAN | `192.168.1.0/24` |
| WireGuard VPN network | `10.10.10.0/24` |
| OPNsense WireGuard interface | `10.10.10.1` |
| CachyOS WireGuard client | `10.10.10.2/32` |
| WireGuard port | `51820/UDP` |

## 3. CachyOS Split-Tunnel Configuration

The WireGuard client configuration is stored at:

`/etc/wireguard/wg0.conf`

The configuration uses the following settings, with sensitive information replaced by placeholders.

```ini
[Interface]
PrivateKey = <Linux-Client-Private-Key>
Address = 10.10.10.2/32

[Peer]
PublicKey = <OPNsense-WireGuard-Public-Key>
Endpoint = <Home-Public-IP>:51820
AllowedIPs = 10.10.10.0/24, 192.168.1.0/24
PersistentKeepalive = 25
```

